\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {REPA's representation advantage is encoder-routed.} REPA-GearNet wins the fold probes (CATH C/A/T) decisively, while REPA-MPNN edges the per-residue probe (IF). The random control gains least and does not help IF, evidence of genuine structural transfer rather than regularisation. (Means over $n{=}3$ seeds at a single 1.0M checkpoint; the seed spread is small on IF and CATH (dihedral is noisier). Best-layer linear probe at $n_\text  {train}{=}1000$ (protocol in Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:leakage}). Per-seed ranges and the remaining variants are in Appendix Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:proteina-rep-full}.)}}{39}{table.6.2}}
