\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Most REPA variants accelerate generation quality over the baseline.} In some regimes they also win the long run. Acceleration is the \%-delta vs the baseline at 400K (the anchor of Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:proteina-genrep}), with the absolute score in parentheses; the long run is each variant's absolute best, with the baseline capped at the furthest trained variant per regime (2.0M PDB, 1.5M AFDB), coloured against the baseline-best row. ($n{=}1$--$3$ seeds, seed-mean; $1{,}125$ backbones/seed, $250$ for designability.)}}{41}{table.6.3}}
\newlabel{tab:proteina-speedup}{{6.3}{41}{\textbf {Most REPA variants accelerate generation quality over the baseline.} In some regimes they also win the long run. Acceleration is the \%-delta vs the baseline at 400K (the anchor of Figure~\ref {fig:proteina-genrep}), with the absolute score in parentheses; the long run is each variant's absolute best, with the baseline capped at the furthest trained variant per regime (2.0M PDB, 1.5M AFDB), coloured against the baseline-best row. ($n{=}1$--$3$ seeds, seed-mean; $1{,}125$ backbones/seed, $250$ for designability.)}{table.6.3}{}}
