\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {On PDB, REPA concentrates the $\beta $-rich designable folds onto fewer modes; on AFDB it does not.} The effect is specific to the most $\beta $-rich bin ($\beta {\ge }25$): PDB-L9-MPNN climbs from $0.29$ (400K) to $0.69$ (1.3M) while its baseline diversifies to $0.13$. Lower-$\beta $ bins and AFDB-L4-GearNet barely move. Designable-subset pairwise TM, lower\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}=\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}more diverse; columns bin by $\beta $-strand fraction (\%). Cells pool the designable subset across all available seeds (2--3 per cell) and the five generation lengths. The $\beta {\ge }25$ bin at 1.3M holds $n{=}188$ designable backbones for REPA-L9-MPNN against $n{=}20$ for the baseline; the sparser 400K $\beta {\ge }25$ bins ($n{\approx }11$--$19$) are directional.)}}{45}{table.6.7}}
\newlabel{tab:proteina-concentration}{{6.7}{45}{\textbf {On PDB, REPA concentrates the $\beta $-rich designable folds onto fewer modes; on AFDB it does not.} The effect is specific to the most $\beta $-rich bin ($\beta {\ge }25$): PDB-L9-MPNN climbs from $0.29$ (400K) to $0.69$ (1.3M) while its baseline diversifies to $0.13$. Lower-$\beta $ bins and AFDB-L4-GearNet barely move. Designable-subset pairwise TM, lower\,=\,more diverse; columns bin by $\beta $-strand fraction (\%). Cells pool the designable subset across all available seeds (2--3 per cell) and the five generation lengths. The $\beta {\ge }25$ bin at 1.3M holds $n{=}188$ designable backbones for REPA-L9-MPNN against $n{=}20$ for the baseline; the sparser 400K $\beta {\ge }25$ bins ($n{\approx }11$--$19$) are directional.)}{table.6.7}{}}
