\newlabel{tab:proteina-rep-full}{{A.3}{58}{\textbf {Full PDB representation-quality ablation across all six variants.} The remaining encoder$\times $depth combinations behind Table~\ref {tab:proteina-rep}, at the same 1.0M checkpoint. The encoder-routed pattern holds: GearNet wins the fold probes (CATH C/A/T), ProteinMPNN edges the inverse-folding probe (IF). At matched layer~4, the trained GearNet (L4-GearNet) beats the random control (L4-random) on every probe, so the learned-versus-random gap is not an artefact of injection depth. (Baseline absolute, REPA rows $\Delta $-from-baseline, $\pm $ half the seed range where $>1$ seed; $n{=}3$ seeds except ($^{\dagger }$) L4-GearNet and L4-MPNN single-seed. Best-layer linear probe at $n_\text {train}{=}1000$.)}{table.A.3}{}}
